<p class=MsoNormal><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'>Installation: </span></b><span style='font-size:10.0pt'><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>Download ReadPlate3.0.txt and
do Plugins &gt; Install. The plugin is ready to be launched by <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>clicking</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> Plugins &gt;ReadPlate3.0 <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>An example image of a 96-well
plate is available at <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'><a
href="../../macros/images/plate.jpg">../../macros/images/plate.jpg</a>
<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'>Description: <o:p></o:p></span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'>Image acquisition: </span></b><span style='font-size:
10.0pt'><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>The multi-well plate is
located on top of a home-built trans-illuminator: a white 7 x 10 LED array, <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>powered</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> by a 12V DC power supply, covered with an acrylic
plate that acts as a light-diffusing <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>base</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> (<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Figure A</b>).
To avoid the influence of stray light, the device is covered with a tall black <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>plywood</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> pyramidal box equipped with a central hole at the top
(<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Figure B</b>), through which the <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>zoom</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> lens of the camera is located (Nikon <span
class=SpellE>CoolPix</span> S6300 in our case, but cell-phone cameras can be <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>used</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> as well). The vertical optical axis passes through
the center of the plate. To minimize parallax <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>error</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> that would affect the light path through the samples,
pictures are taken at a minimal distance <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>of</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> 70 cm. The plate borders should be parallel to the
frame of the picture. The example <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>photograph</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> (stored as a .jpg file) corresponds to a 96-well
plate with samples of a colorimetric <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>assay</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> for lactate (120 <span class=SpellE>&#956;L</span>
per well, maximum of absorbance at 555 nm). In this case, the green <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>channel</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> shows the highest sensitivity, due to maximal spectral
overlap between the absorption <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>spectrum</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> of the <span class=SpellE>chromophore</span> in the
sample and the green window. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'>Plugin use: </span></b><span style='font-size:10.0pt'><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>Before starting (very
important!), please set the following parameters for measurements: <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>(Analyze &gt; Set
Measurements). The following should be selected: Area / Standard Deviation / <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>Min &amp; Max Gray Value/
Mean Gray Value/ Modal Gray Value/ Add to Overlay / Redirect to None / <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>Decimal Places (0-9): 3. <span
class=SpellE>ReadPlate</span> measures the color intensity (RGB) of an image
(.jpg file) of a <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>multi</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'>-well plate of 6 (3x2), 12 (4x3), 24 (6x4), 48 (8x6)
or 96 (12x8) wells. The color photograph <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>of</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> the plate should be centered at the middle point. For
further details and validation against a <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>commercial</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> plate reader, see the Supplementary Material (Figure
S3) of the literature reference <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>cited</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> above. Open the .jpg image from within the <span
class=SpellE>ImageJ</span> software (tested with version 1.53c, <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>Wayne <span class=SpellE>Rasband</span>,
NIH, 26 June 2020). Run the plugin <span class=SpellE>ReadPlate</span> (by
launching Plugins &gt; <span class=SpellE>ReadPlate</span>). <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>Select the correct plate
format: 6(3x2), 12(4x3), 24(6x4), 48(8x6) or 96(12x8) wells (<b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Figure C</b>). <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>Make a center-to-center
rectangular selection of wells (upper-left and lower-right corners, <b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Figure D</b>). <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>Select the desired color
channel (Red, Green, Blue or Gray) for measurements (<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
normal'>Figure E</b>). Choose <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>the</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> appropriate parameters for the grid of circles to be
measured (<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Figure F</b>). Each circle
needs <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>not</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> be too large, because enough color information is
coded in pixels covering a relatively small <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>area</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'>. The final grid overlaid on the plate should show main
circles centered on each well surrounded <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>by</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> ancillary circles located outside (<b
style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Figure G</b>). The latter are used by the
blank correction <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>algorithm</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> to compensate for any difference in local light
intensity (<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Figure H</b>). Check the fit
of the <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>final</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> grid onto the plate image. If satisfactory, the user
proceeds to collect measurements. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>A table of results will
appear next (<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Figure I</b>). This
includes number, alphanumeric <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>label</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> and area of each well, light intensity measurements
(Mean, <span class=SpellE>StdDev</span>, Mode, Min, Max), <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>and</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> absorbance values. Corrected absorbance values (<span
class=SpellE>Acorr</span>) result from applying the blank <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>suppression</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> algorithm. Note that <i style='mso-bidi-font-style:
normal'>all measurements are taken on a single image of the plate</i>, thus <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span class=GramE><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>eliminating</span></span><span
style='font-size:10.0pt'> the need for taking parallel measurements on an empty
plate. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:10.0pt'>By default, results are
formatted as .<span class=SpellE>csv</span> files, readily interpretable by
Excel (<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Figure J</b>). <o:p></o:p></span></p>

